# SPA rewrites: each client-side route serves index.html so React Router
# can render it. The 200 status makes these server-side rewrites, not
# redirects — the URL in the browser stays the same.
#
# The target is `/`, not `/index.html`: Pages' pretty-URL handling answers a
# rewrite to /index.html with a 308 redirect to `/`, which would bounce
# every deep link to the home page (verified with `wrangler pages dev`).
#
# This is deliberately an allowlist, not a `/*` catch-all. Any path not
# listed here (and not a real static file) falls through to dist/404.html,
# which Cloudflare Pages serves with a genuine 404 status. A catch-all would
# answer every junk URL with 200 OK (a "soft 404").
#
# Every <Route path> in src/main.tsx must have a rule here, or production
# serves that page as a 404. src/routes.test.ts enforces this.
/battle               /             200
/builder              /             200
/learn                /             200
/leaderboard          /             200
/profile              /             200
/users/:username      /             200
/lobby                /             200
/match/:matchId       /             200
